  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A small CRT with excessive enthusiasm",
    "overview": "The original charcoal CRT, crooked antenna, ivory gloves, orange sneakers and tiny photograph carry the expression. Its ink outlines and raster geometry remain the visual identity. Acid-lime phosphor and saturated geometric effects make its actions readable against both a quiet review stage and a photograph.\n\nThe inspection page is warm, spare and orderly: condensed display lettering, dark green-black text, ruled controls and restrained vermilion. The page supplies a calm frame for an animated character whose anticipation, mishaps and recovery supply the humor. Preserve the approved artwork and choreography when extending this system.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Original outlined raster character with neon color baked into its assets.",
      "Warm neutral stages and a dark simulated camera frame.",
      "Condensed display type paired with plain functional body text.",
      "Three authored arrivals and departures sharing one five-second performance.",
      "One inspection clock for pictures, bounded effects and sound."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Baked Color Rule",
